From 7d9e29863c69a2dd37d6766412d0c8181a705ca3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Isaac Duarte <31712685+Isaac-Duarte@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:22:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 24/32] arm64: dts: apple: t6050-j714s: let userspace set the
 fan speeds

Mark both J714s fans apple,fan-manual-control, as the M4 Pro/Max
MacBook Pros and the J704 already are, so fanX_target is writable
without the unsafe fan_control module parameter. The SMC still drives
the fans until userspace writes a target, and writing 0 hands a fan
back to the firmware. The M5 GPU governor already sets these fans
through the same manual mode; a userspace target takes a fan over from
it until 0 is written.

Under bursty CPU load the firmware's curve leaves both fans at their
idle speed (targets about 2320/2500 rpm) while the SoC hotspot (TCMb)
reaches 105-111 C and the firmware lowers the CPU clocks. Faster fans
set from userspace recover much of it: a clean Rust release build
drops from 60 s to 47 s with the fans at their maximum. With the
fan_control parameter on this machine, both fans took a manual speed
and returned to the firmware's curve after 0 was written; that is the
same driver path this property enables.

J716s and J775D are left as they are until their fans are tested the
same way.

Tested on J714s (7.3.0-36.n1usb) with its installed device tree plus
this property and fan_control=N: both fanX_target are 0644, the kernel
is not tainted, fan 1 set to 4000 rpm ran at 3996 rpm and returned to
the firmware's idle speed (2326 rpm) after 0 was written, with no
macsmc-hwmon warnings.

Signed-off-by: Isaac Duarte <31712685+Isaac-Duarte@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-j714s.dts | 17 ++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-j714s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-j714s.dts
index b1dcc1d9d98f..9e565552c9c3 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-j714s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-j714s.dts
@@ -599,10 +599,10 @@ &jpeg1 {
 #include "t6050-j714s-pmp-tunables.dtsi"
 
 /*
- * SMC sensors, as on J716s: the shared fan, power, voltage and current keys, plus
- * every readable float T* key through apple,discover-temperatures in
- * t6050-die0.dtsi, labelled with the key name. A key this SMC lacks only drops
- * its channel.
+ * SMC sensors, as on J716s except that userspace may set the fans (below): the
+ * shared fan, power, voltage and current keys, plus every readable float T* key
+ * through apple,discover-temperatures in t6050-die0.dtsi, labelled with the key
+ * name. A key this SMC lacks only drops its channel.
  *
  * Discovery refuses to run once any temperature channel exists, so the shared
  * temperature nodes go (their keys are discovered anyway), and so does
@@ -620,13 +620,20 @@ &smc_hwmon {
 	/delete-node/ temperature-TCHP;
 	/delete-node/ temperature-TW0P;
 
-	/* The T6050 SMC spells the fan mode keys F0md/F1md. The SMC drives the fans. */
+	/*
+	 * The T6050 SMC spells the fan mode keys F0md/F1md. The SMC drives the
+	 * fans (the M5 GPU governor sets them through macsmc_hwmon_fans_request()
+	 * as well); it also accepts a manual speed for both from userspace and
+	 * returns them to firmware control when the request is dropped.
+	 */
 	fan-F0Ac {
 		apple,fan-mode = "F0md";
+		apple,fan-manual-control;
 	};
 
 	fan-F1Ac {
 		apple,fan-mode = "F1md";
+		apple,fan-manual-control;
 	};
 };
 
